    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fitting Multiple Classess in one.]]></title>
        <id>http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses</id>
        <link href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses"/>
        <updated>2022-06-09T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[Idea: What if I run out of things to teach? I can teach multiple things that the students might be williing to learn.]]></summary>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h2 class="anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id="idea-what-if-i-run-out-of-things-to-teach-i-can-teach-multiple-things-that-the-students-might-be-williing-to-learn">Idea: What if I run out of things to teach? I can teach multiple things that the students might be williing to learn.<a href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses#idea-what-if-i-run-out-of-things-to-teach-i-can-teach-multiple-things-that-the-students-might-be-williing-to-learn" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Idea: What if I run out of things to teach? I can teach multiple things that the students might be williing to learn." title="Direct link to Idea: What if I run out of things to teach? I can teach multiple things that the students might be williing to learn.">​</a></h2>
<p><strong>Reasoning</strong>
Usually my "lecture" takes around 5 minutes. The rest of the class is left for students to work on the activity</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id="strategy">Strategy<a href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses#strategy" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Strategy" title="Direct link to Strategy">​</a></h2>
<ul>
<li>Separate the lesson of 45 minutes in order to fit multiple lectures.</li>
<li>Separate the different lessons  the further apart from each other so it's not a "lump" of information</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id="what-to-learn">What to learn?<a href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses#what-to-learn" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What to learn?" title="Direct link to What to learn?">​</a></h2>
<h3 class="anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id="intro">Intro<a href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses#intro" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Intro" title="Direct link to Intro">​</a></h3>
<ul>
<li>Python basics</li>
<li>UX Design</li>
<li>3D Modeling and Printing.</li>
<li>Art for Videogames: Pixel Art + Animations</li>
<li>Mobile App Dev MIT App Inventor</li>
<li>Java</li>
<li>Game Development using GameStudio 2</li>
<li>Web Development (Front-end)</li>
<li>Crafts 101</li>
<li>Javascript</li>
<li>Ethics, Commuinication and Project Managament for engineers</li>
<li>Relational Databases</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_LWe7" id="after-the-first-programming-language">After the first programming Language<a href="http://learn.wangnelson.xyz/blog/2022/6/9/fitting-multiple-courses#after-the-first-programming-language" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to After the first programming Language" title="Direct link to After the first programming Language">​</a></h3>
<p>Requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Needs a Windows/Mac Laptop</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Have learn Python or Java first</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Dungeon and Dragons + Python.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Python for boring stuff Automation</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Python Advanced</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Hardware and Robotics</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Data Science &amp; Artificial Intelligence</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Hacking 101</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Competitive Programming</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Cracking your code Interview</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Game Development using Unity (Fairly Hard)</p>
</li>
</ul>
